<title>USA: TENNIS-BAUSCH &amp; LOMB CHAMPIONSHIPS WOMEN'S RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-BAUSCH &amp; LOMB CHAMPIONSHIPS WOMEN'S RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>AMELIA ISLAND, Florida 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results at the</p>
<p>$450,000 Bausch &amp; Lomb Championships women's tennis tournament</p>
<p>on Wednesday (prefix number denotes seeding):</p>
<p>Second round</p>
<p>1-Jana Novotna (Czech Republic) beat Barbara Schett (Austria)</p>
<p>4-6 6-4 6-0</p>
<p>8-Iva Majoli (Croatia) beat Angeles Montolio (Spain) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>9-Mary Joe Fernandez (U.S.) beat Patricia Hy-Boulais (Canada)</p>
<p>6-3 6-0</p>
<p>11-Mary Pierce (France) beat Henrieta Nagyova (Slovakia) 7-5</p>
<p>6-0</p>
<p>12-Amanda Coetzer (South Africa) beat Amelie Mauresmo</p>
<p>(France) 6-4 1-6 6-1</p>
<p>13-Brenda Schultz-McCarthy (Netherlands) beat Sandra Kleinova</p>
<p>(Czech Republic) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Alexandra Fusai (France) beat 14-Elena Likhovtseva (Russia)</p>
<p>1-6 7-6 (7-1) 6-4</p>
<p>Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania) beat Ann Grossman (U.S.) 6-2 6-3</p>
<p>Chanda Rubin (U.S.) beat Venus Williams (U.S.) 6-4 6-0</p>
<p>Jana Kandarr (Germany) beat Silvia Farina (Italy) 6-4 7-6</p>
<p>(7-4)</p>
<p>Marlene Weingartner (Germany) beat Tatjana Jecmenica</p>
<p>(Yugoslavia) 2-6 7-6 (7-3) 7-5</p>
</text>
